1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Hello everyone, in this tutorial video, we will learn about some adjustments we need to make to virtual models before we really start making clothes.

2
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:28,000
First of all, in our software, if you want to use a virtual model, you can import this virtual model in the form of FBX or OBJ.

3
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Here we import a FBX file.

4
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
After importing the FBX file, there are some options at the bottom.

5
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
The first option is the object you imported, and the second option is the proportion you imported.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,000
The proportion is actually the unit of the imported object.

7
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Everyone must pay attention to the units.

8
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:52,000
For example, here I imported a relatively small unit when I imported the model and imported it as mm.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Because the default input unit of our software is mm.

10
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,000
After importing, compare the ground network grid.

11
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,000
This is the ground network grid.

12
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,000
This model is relatively small.

13
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Because the units we import into the model are relatively small,

14
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:10,000
some of the default settings in the software, including surface rigidity, rendering thickness, and collision thickness,

15
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,000
their basic units are mm.

16
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:18,000
In this case, if we use this model to create a version,

17
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:25,000
then if we open the grid display here, you will see that its grid number is actually very small.

18
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,000
In this case,

19
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,000
we can't make a version on it.

20
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Because its grid number is too small.

21
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:38,000
The reason why the grid number is small is because our default particle diameter is 20 mm.

22
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:41,000
That is to say, one edge of a grid is 20 mm.

23
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:46,000
If we forcefully reduce its particle diameter for this model,

24
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:48,000
even if it is reduced to 5,

25
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:51,000
because now one edge is still 5 mm,

26
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,000
its transition is still not smooth enough.

27
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,000
And when we put the version on this virtual model,

28
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,000
because the virtual model is imported,

29
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:03,000
its surface rigidity is default set to 3 mm.

30
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:06,000
Therefore, compared to the size of this version,

31
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,000
it seems that this air thickness is particularly thick.

32
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Therefore, after we import a model,

33
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,000
we must make sure that its ratio is correct.

34
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:19,000
Next, let's take a look at what happens if we choose a larger ratio.

35
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Compared to the ground network grid, we can see that

36
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:28,000
the ground network grid is significantly higher than the ground network grid after its arms are opened.

37
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:30,000
If it is a normal proportion model,

38
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:34,000
its arms are not higher than the ground network grid.

39
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Then we can see that if we rely on the modeling of the model to draw the version,

40
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:44,000
this version will be a larger version.

41
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Therefore, even if the particle diameter is 20 mm,

42
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,000
its network grid is also a lot.

43
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:51,000
If we start the simulation to simulate this version,

44
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,000
the computer will run very slowly.

45
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:59,000
If you are not sure what the unit of the model you want to import is,

46
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:02,000
you can open the virtual model you brought in our software,

47
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:05,000
and then use this virtual model as reference,

48
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:08,000
and then choose its unit.

49
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
After importing HANA,

50
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:14,000
you will find that this model is much larger compared to HANA.

51
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,000
That means that when we choose a unit,

52
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:20,000
we have to choose a unit that is one level smaller than this unit.

53
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Now, after determining the unit,

54
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:27,000
we can import the model first.

55
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:33,000
Because we originally chose millimeters and inches,

56
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:36,000
here we choose a centimeter.

57
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:39,000
In addition to importing units,

58
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,000
we also have a proportion when importing.

59
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:46,000
If you need to do a certain reduction of this proportion because of your own settings,

60
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,000
it is also possible.

61
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,000
After importing the virtual model,

62
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
if you import an FBX file,

63
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:56,000
it may not automatically generate the layout and layout points.

64
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Now that we have talked about the layout and layout points,

65
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:03,000
let's take a look at some settings about the virtual model display.

66
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,000
First of all, the first one is to display the virtual model.

67
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:06,000
This is very simple.

68
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:10,000
It means to display all virtual models or hide all virtual models.

69
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Then we can choose the display layout point and display layout board.

70
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:17,000
Here, because there is no layout point or layout board around the virtual model,

71
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,000
it will not be displayed.

72
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,000
After selecting display X-ray,

73
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:25,000
it will display the virtual model's own Google joint information.

74
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,000
After selecting a joint point,

75
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:33,000
we can rotate the layout or move the layout to rotate and move this Google.

76
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:36,000
If the FBX file with the layout is imported,

77
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:39,000
a prompt will pop up to remind you.

78
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:42,000
If you modify the joint point or the Google point,

79
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:46,000
the animation brought by this file will disappear.

80
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:48,000
Should we continue?

81
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Yes.

82
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,000
Then we can rotate the layout or move the layout

83
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:58,000
to adjust the virtual model's posture after selecting the joint point.

84
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:00,000
When we select a joint point,

85
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:04,000
there is an option of symmetrical editing on the upper right of the layout.

86
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:07,000
If you click on it, it means that the symmetrical editing is opened.

87
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:09,000
After clicking on this button,

88
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:11,000
the layout will disappear.

89
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,000
Its moving option is only rotating,

90
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:16,000
and all rotating operations are symmetrical.

91
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Of course, only in the original set layout,

92
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:21,000
the name of the initial set joint symmetry point is corresponding,

93
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:24,000
so that symmetrical editing can be carried out.

94
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:27,000
If your joint point can not be linked to the left and right together,

95
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:30,000
please first confirm in other software

96
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:34,000
whether your joint point is set to the name is corresponding to each other.

97
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:37,000
After selecting display virtual model size,

98
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,000
the size information on the virtual model will be displayed.

99
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:45,000
This size information is required for us to use the basic length measurement in advance,

100
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,000
or the basic circle measurement, etc.

101
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:50,000
The choice of virtual model measurement

102
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:54,000
will be displayed only after creating a measurement line.

103
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,000
For example, here,

104
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:57,000
when I create a virtual model measurement,

105
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:00,000
if I switch back to select the moving tool,

106
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:01,000
it will not be displayed,

107
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:05,000
unless I choose to display virtual model measurement information here.

108
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:10,000
The next option is to display the line virtual model.

109
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:13,000
If you want to display the line virtual model,

110
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:16,000
first we need to create the line virtual model.

111
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,000
After using the line virtual model tool,

112
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:23,000
click on the virtual model and create a point.

113
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:24,000
During the process,

114
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:26,000
press the Ctrl key to create a curve point.

115
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:28,000
When we use the line virtual model,

116
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:32,000
this shape created becomes a closed shape,

117
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:36,000
use the flattening tool to select this closed shape,

118
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:39,000
then press the Enter key to remove the sheet.

119
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:42,000
The removed sheet can be used as a basic sheet,

120
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:44,000
and be modified above.

121
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:45,000
If we want to adjust these lines,

122
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:48,000
we can use the edit line virtual model tool

123
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,000
to adjust its point or straight line.

124
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Double-click on a point to select the entire shape,

125
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:56,000
press the Delete key to delete the entire shape.

126
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:57,000
In the default situation,

127
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:00,000
we use other tools that can't see the line virtual model.

128
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:03,000
The next one is to display the virtual model.

129
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:07,000
The default virtual model does not have a virtual model information,

130
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:09,000
and the virtual model information is that

131
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:13,000
we can use the virtual model information of different virtual models

132
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:16,000
to automatically adapt or automate the sheet.

133
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:17,000
In the 3D tool bar,

134
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,000
after selecting to create a point,

135
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:21,000
if there is a sheet in your 3D space,

136
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,000
it will remind you whether the file is not yet saved.

137
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:26,000
Remember to save it here.

138
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:29,000
Then we can start to measure the size of the virtual models

139
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:31,000
to create a point.

140
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:33,000
When creating a point,

141
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:36,000
you can use the information chart of this point

142
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,000
to draw the virtual model

143
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,000
based on its high position.

144
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:42,000
This is the same as the virtual model measurement.

145
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Click, click, click,

146
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:47,000
and then click three points to determine a circle line.

147
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,000
First is the top view,

148
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:50,000
then the bottom view,

149
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:52,000
then the waist,

150
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,000
and then step by step to create a point.

151
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:56,000
During the creation process,

152
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,000
press the Shift key

153
00:07:57,000 --> 00:08:00,000
to create those points along the level or value direction.

154
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:03,000
When you have created all the measurements,

155
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:04,000
click on the application,

156
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,000
the virtual model will be worn on the virtual model,

157
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:08,000
just like what I drew.

158
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,000
We will see that the virtual model

159
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:11,000
is actually a particularly tight deep red color,

160
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:13,000
so we will use the dark red clothing information.

161
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:15,000
Through the virtual model table,

162
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:17,000
this layer of red clothing information,

163
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,000
we can achieve different body shapes

164
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:21,000
of the virtual model's clothing accessories.

165
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,000
If you want to delete a piece of information,

166
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,000
select this information,

167
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,000
then press the Delete key

168
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,000
to rewrite this part of the information.

169
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,000
In other words,

170
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:31,000
you can re-create the measurement.

171
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:32,000
After the modification,

172
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,000
you need to click on the application again

173
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,000
to apply the clothing.

174
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,000
If your model is not symmetrical on the left and right,

175
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,000
here we can cancel the selection of its symmetry.

176
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,000
If you click on the application,

177
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:43,000
you will find that there is a small difference.

178
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,000
We can manually drag it

179
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:47,000
to make the whole dress more flat.

180
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:50,000
Finally, remember to save this virtual model

181
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:53,000
to allow the virtual model to have the dress information.

182
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,000
After that,

183
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,000
we will look at another

184
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,000
menu bar related to virtual models.

185
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,000
Here we can change the virtual model

186
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:03,000
to black and white surface or grid display.

187
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,000
Another point is that

188
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:07,000
all the models that are imported to our software,

189
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,000
its grid type

190
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:10,000
will eventually be automatically adjusted

191
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,000
to a triangular grid.

192
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:12,000
That's it for some basic knowledge

193
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,000
about import.

